---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SubmitForm from '../../components/SubmitForm.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Propose a glossary"
  description="Jargonautica is meant to be a family of glossaries. Artificial intelligence is the first. Tell us which field should be next."
>
  <h1>Propose a glossary</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The two-level format is not specific to artificial intelligence. It suits any field that invents
    vocabulary faster than it explains it, which is most of them. AI is the first glossary and it is not
    meant to be the last.
  </p>

  <SubmitForm kind="glossary" />

  <h2>What This Actually Takes</h2>
  <p>
    Worth being honest about the size of it. The AI glossary is 477 entries, each written twice, each
    linked to the ones it depends on. It took a while. A glossary is not a weekend.
  </p>
  <p>
    Which is why the last question on that form is the one that matters. A subject nobody is willing to
    help with is a subject that stays a good idea. A subject with someone who knows it well enough to
    argue about the definitions is a subject that can actually happen.
  </p>
</Base>
